# SPA routing for Netlify and Cloudflare Pages.
#
# RepX uses BrowserRouter, so /play, /privacy and /delete-account are real URLs
# that the static host has no file for. Without this rule a hard refresh or a
# pasted link returns 404 — including the /verify and /reset links sent by
# email, and the /privacy and /delete-account URLs submitted to Google Play.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. The catch-all is last, and the exclusions above it exist
# because a blanket rewrite silently serves index.html for them:
#
#   assetlinks.json  Chrome would receive HTML where it expects JSON, fail
#                    verification, and the Play app would show a URL bar with no
#                    obvious cause. This is the most common TWA failure there is.
#   sw.js            A service worker served as HTML fails to register, taking
#                    offline support with it.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the browser must keep the original URL so the router can
# read it. A redirect would rewrite the address bar to / and lose the token in a
# password-reset link.

/.well-known/assetlinks.json   /.well-known/assetlinks.json   200
/sw.js                         /sw.js                         200
/manifest.webmanifest          /manifest.webmanifest          200

/*                             /index.html                    200
